### Install the mergefs
```
sudo apt update
sudo apt install mergerfs
```

### Check the SSDs which are already mounted with strange name
```lsblk```

### Find the SSDs and umount them
For example, 
```sudo umount “/media/atlas/Crucial X10”```

### Setup new mount
```
sudo mkdir -p /mnt/hdd0
sudo mkdir -p /mnt/hdd1
sudo mkdir -p /mnt/hdd2
```

### Find the UUID and the TYPE
```
sudo blkid
```
### Change the /etc/fstab file
Add these lines.
NEED TO CHANGE THE UUID, and the TYPE
```
UUID=a1b2c3d4-e5f6-7890-abcd-ef1234567890  /mnt/hdd0  ext4  defaults,nofail  0  2
UUID=b2c3d4e5-f6a7-8901-bcde-f12345678901  /mnt/hdd1  ext4  defaults,nofail  0  2
UUID=b2c3d4e5-f6a7-8901-bcde-f12345678901  /mnt/hdd2  ext4  defaults,nofail  0  2
```

### MUST CHECK!! IF ISSUES, THE MACHINE WILL NOT REBOOT ANYMORE
```
sudo systemctl daemon-reload
sudo mount -a  # NOTHING SHOULD BE OUTPUT
df -h /mnt/hdd0 /mnt/hdd1 /mnt/hdd2
```

### Merge
```
sudo mkdir -p /mnt/storage
sudo nano /etc/fstab

# add merge command
/mnt/hdd0:/mnt/hdd1:/mnt/hdd2  /mnt/storage  mergerfs  allow_other,cache.files=off,category.create=epmfs,func.getattr=newest,dropcacheonclose=false,minfreespace=100G 0 0

sudo nano /etc/fuse.con # set #user_allow_other to user_allow_other
```

###  MUST CHECK AGAIN!! IF ISSUES, THE MACHINE WILL NOT REBOOT ANYMORE
```
sudo systemctl daemon-reload
sudo mount -a  # NOTHING SHOULD BE OUTPUT
df -h /mnt/storage
```

### Run the test scripts.
```
python3 test_ssd.py
```